<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keys merged into the generated Info.plist by tauri-bundler
  (bundle.macOS.infoPlist). User keys OVERRIDE generated ones, so keep this
  file to the minimum we actually need — anything added here shadows whatever
  Tauri would have produced.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Opt out of App Nap.

    This app is not a foreground-only UI. It hosts the loopback relay that
    carries the agent's node traffic: the backend pushes a connect.challenge
    down over the API Gateway socket THIS process owns, and it forwards the
    frame to the bundled openclaw-host subprocess, which signs it. Backgrounded
    and idle, macOS demotes us to the background QoS band and that forwarding
    stalls for seconds.

    Measured on a live 0.4.53 install (2026-08-03), scheduling priority:

        backgrounded  lightbulb-desktop = 4    openclaw-node = 31
        foregrounded  lightbulb-desktop = 46   openclaw-node = 31

    Only the relay is throttled; the signer is unaffected. Prod API Gateway
    logs caught the consequence — a challenge pushed at 23:08:23 and signed at
    23:08:36, 13s later, with backend integrationLatency of 111ms. The whole
    delay was this process waiting to be scheduled.

    The backend budget for that round trip is 30s (raised from 10s, which had
    turned a routine background app into a permanent reconnect flap), but the
    budget is tolerance, not the fix. A relay for a remote agent must stay
    responsive while the window is behind something else, which is the normal
    case for this app.

    NOT NSActivityIdleSystemSleepDisabled: this suppresses App Nap only and
    deliberately does not hold the machine awake. If a future macOS ignores
    this key from a bundle, the equivalent is an NSProcessInfo activity
    assertion with .userInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep held for the lifetime
    of the node connection — same intent, needs Obj-C interop the crate does
    not currently have.
  -->
  <key>NSAppSleepDisabled</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
